  "limitations": [
    "Bounded Conway/PV9 GOV and PV11 lawful RATIFY integration observations; not a full generator campaign or all governance action families.",
    "Five retained GOV environments encode zero registration counts as NonZero Word64. Native constrained generation and in-memory execution accept these, but they violate the native CBOR reader and Scarab typed domain. These are explicit unsupported cases, not full-state matches.",
    "The original RATIFY integration is unmodified apart from observation. Other RATIFY cases use the same native lawful setup with positive 1/2 DRep and SPO thresholds; competing proposals differ only in supplied order.",
    "Missing-vote RATIFY is an accepted transition retaining unratified actions, distinct from GOV predicate rejection.",
    "GOV deposit refusal compares native/formal rejection statuses and the original native ProposalDepositIncorrect payload against Scarab structured error. Formal rejection text is not required to match.",
    "Native trace CBOR is not a persisted Scarab snapshot format. No persisted format changes.",
    "All ten representable generated GOV samples name voters with empty inner vote maps; seven also submit proposals. These exercise nonempty signal/proposal handling and voter existence, not recording votes onto actions. RATIFY integration carries genuine yes votes but does not separately establish GOV cast-vote conformance."
